@testray.main.component.name = "Support QA"

Feature: DXP Trial
	Testing the DXP Trial page.

Setup:
	* I go to the DXP Trial Sign In page
	* I generate a web user email address
	* I generate a web company name
	* I create a DXP trial account with a randomly generated email address and company name with the following additional values
	| Email        | ${staticEmailAddress}               |
	| Password     | testtest                            |
	| First Name   | DXP                                 |
	| Last Name    | Trialuser                           |
	| Phone Number | 555-555-5555                        |
	| Company      | ${staticCompanyName}                |
	| Industry     | Automotive                          |
	| Country      | United States                       |
	| Region       | California                          |

Teardown:
	* I wait for "10" seconds
	* I get the web corporate trial organziation id value with the name "${staticCompanyName}" belonging to the user with the email address "${staticEmailAddress}"
	* I tear down the users with the following email addresses from web.liferay.com
	| ${staticEmailAddress} |
	* I tear down the web corporate trial organization with the ID value "${staticTrialOrganizationIdValue}"
	* I log out and log into the support homepage as "amos.fong@liferay.com.broken" with password "test"
	* I tear down the projects with the following project names
	| Trial - ${staticCompanyName} |
	* I delete the support email message in MockMock where the sender is "Liferay" the recipient is "DXP Trialuser" with the email address "${staticEmailAddress}" and the message content contains the text "Trial Activation Key"

Scenario: View DXP Trial User
	Trial users should have specific parameters and privileges.

	* I should be able to the view the DXP Trial Homepage
	* the user with the email address "${staticEmailAddress}" should be part of the web Trial organization
	* the user with the email address "${staticEmailAddress}" should be part of the web corporate trial organization for the company "${staticCompanyName}"
	* I log into the support homepage as "amos.fong@liferay.com.broken" with password "test"
	* I go to the OSB admin main page
	* I view a project with the name "Trial - ${staticCompanyName}" and following values
	| Name         | Trial - ${staticCompanyName} |
	| Code         | TRIALCOMPANY                 |
	| Type         | Trial                        |
	| Industry     | Automotive                   |
	| Tier         | Regular                      |
	| Max Contacts | 1                            |
	| Country      | United States                |
	* I view a project offering for the project "Trial - ${staticCompanyName}" with a product name "Digital Enterprise Development" and the following values
	| Status           | Active                         |
	| Type             | Trial                          |
	| Product          | Digital Enterprise Development |
	| SLA              | Limited                        |
	| Start Date       | Today                          |
	| Support End Date | 1 month from now               |
	| Version          | 7                              |
	| Instance Size    | Sizing 1                       |
	| Licenses         | 1 / 10000                      |
	| Tickets          | 0                              |
	* I go the support email message in MockMock where the sender is "Liferay" the recipient is "DXP Trialuser" with the email address "${staticEmailAddress}" and the message content contains the text "Trial Activation Key"